{
 "spec": "design specs/PROP_LIBRARY.md v0.1 \u00a75 A, B and D (master fc7c131); placements from specs/prop_library_rooms.py HOME_ADD, FERN_ADD and BATH_ADD, with the one-cell nudges in the notes below. \u00a75 C (the Brightgate HQ lobby, D2034) is held and not built.",
 "_about": "PROP_DRESS (D2032, D2033, D2035; red, Vincent said yes to home_before_after.png, bath_before_after.png and fernbrook_before_after.png on Wed Nov 4, 2026; D2034, the Brightgate HQ lobby, is held and not in this file). A detail pass with the prop library art (PROP_LIBRARY_ART in sprites.js): props and walkable decals only, no grid row, no resize (D84), no reshape (D81). interiors.json, fernbrook_rooms.json and the Kilnmouth and Brightgate overlays stay as they are (Brightgate's lobby is untouched). A prop's (x, y) is its blocking cell: a 1-wide, 2-tall prop (the Keeper lamps) sits on its base cell and draws over the cell above; a wider prop is one slice <id>_n per cell. Nothing here is tappable (no lines). Named detail_zzzzzz_ so it applies after every other overlay, as the previews did. Save stays pixelpets.save.v2, v 2; nothing is written to the save.",
 "_home_note": "One nudge from home_before_after.png: the reading chair stands at (7,4), not (7,3). At (7,3) it takes the only open side of home_bookshelf (7,2), whose lines the player taps (S3: every interactable keeps one free reach cell). One cell down it still sits by the books, beside home_table and home_plant, as a reading group.",
 "_fernbrook_note": "Six one-cell nudges from fernbrook_before_after.png, because the preview's spots shut walkable grass off from the rest of the town, and a save standing there would load with no way out (safeSpot only moves a save off a blocked cell). The orchard stall moves right (28,21 -> 29,21), so the strip behind the stitcher's roof (row 20) opens down x 28; the sacks sit in the corner it frees (30,21 -> 30,20), the crate below the stall (30,22 -> 30,23), the barrels left (28,24 -> 27,24) so x 28 reaches the lane. The flower planter moves left (21,24 -> 20,24) so the grass behind the cart opens at (21,24); the barrow moves left (15,30 -> 14,30) so (15,29) under the wood bench opens. The first Keeper lamp's base is (19,22); its top half draws over fbh_gate_post at (19,21), as in the preview. Decals (tufts, wear, moss) are walkable and may sit on paving (PROP_LIBRARY \u00a72.2 E3); no blocking piece stands on a path tile, door, warp, trigger, sign, NPC or a tap's last open side.",
 "_bath_note": "D2033, Kilnmouth bathhouse (km_bath_in): BATH_ADD as previewed, with one nudge. The second poolside bucket stands at (12,5), not (13,5): #318 put km_notches on the basin's end (13,2) and the mural's tap on the face (14,1), both tapped from (14,2) only, which is reached by the one-wide walk down x 14 from (14,5). At (13,5) the bucket and the bench at (14,6) sealed (14,5), so the walk, both taps and a save standing there were cut off. At (12,5) it still sits poolside, above the bench at (12,6). The first bench (1,6) keeps two of its three tap sides ((2,6), (1,7)) under the preview's bucket at (1,5).",
